# {{project_name}}

A payment splitter that distributes received funds to payees by fixed shares,
generated by
[soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge) from the
`payment-splitter` template.

## How it works

Payees and their shares are fixed at initialization, and payments are *pulled*
rather than pushed:

1. **Deposit** — anyone calls `deposit` to move tokens into the splitter. The
   amount is added to `total_received`.
2. **Entitlement** — each payee has earned
   `total_received * share / total_shares` over the contract's lifetime.
3. **Release** — `release(payee)` transfers what that payee has earned but not
   yet withdrawn. Nothing is transferred on deposit, so one payee can never
   block a payment for the others.

Because entitlements are floor-divided, up to `total_shares - 1` units can sit
in the contract as rounding dust; `undistributed` reports it. The dust is not
lost — later deposits push each entitlement over the next whole unit and it
becomes claimable.

## Interface

| function                            | description                                  |
|-------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `initialize(token, payees, shares)` | fix the payee set and their shares           |
| `deposit(from, amount)`             | move `amount` tokens into the splitter       |
| `releasable(payee)`                 | what the payee can withdraw right now        |
| `release(payee)`                    | transfer everything owed to the payee        |
| `earned(payee)` / `released(payee)` | lifetime entitlement / already withdrawn     |
| `undistributed()`                   | rounding dust still held by the contract     |

## Develop

```sh
cargo test                 # run unit tests
stellar contract build     # build the deployable wasm
```

## Deploy to testnet

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

Then configure the payees and their shares:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <ADMIN> \
  --network testnet \
  -- initialize \
  --token <TOKEN_ADDRESS> \
  --payees '["<PAYEE_A>","<PAYEE_B>"]' \
  --shares '[70,30]'
```

Deposit funds, then let a payee withdraw their cut:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <FUNDER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- deposit --from <FUNDER_ADDRESS> --amount 1000

stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <PAYEE_A> \
  --network testnet \
  -- release --payee <PAYEE_A>
```

